WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.570
My name is Rumen Hristov,
and I'm supervised

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.360
by Professor Dina Katabi.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.750
Device-free sensing has enabled
a variety of systems for health

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.520
monitoring in people's homes.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.680
Our device in
particular is a sensor

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.610
that you attach on the
wall and emits RF signals.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.560
Based on the way these
signals are reflected,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.360
we can localize
the people and see

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.380
whether they're walking, they're
just sitting, or laying in bed.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.107
However, one issue with this is
that we don't know who is who.

00:00:27.107 --> 00:00:28.940
If there are two people
in the environment--

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.220
Bob and Anna-- and one
of them is sleeping

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.840
and the other one
is walking, we don't

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.080
know whether the person who is
walking is Bob or it is Anna.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.260
And this is exactly the problem
that my research is solving.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.250
One major challenge
with this is that we

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.369
need to obtain ground root
label data in people's homes.

00:00:46.369 --> 00:00:48.410
We can't just put cameras
and see what's going on

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.510
and who is who because they
have a big privacy concern.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.240
And our solution is to give
the small accelerometer

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.350
sensor to the person
that we're monitoring.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.230
And we correlate the motion
from the accelerometer sensor

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:02.960
with the output of our device.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.840
In this way we obtain
label data in the homes.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.210
However, the people
wear this sensor

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.860
only for just a couple of days.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.470
And after that,
we're on our own.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.670
Fortunately, people
reflect the RF signals

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.340
in a unique way based on their
body shape or their height.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.220
So we leverage this information
and build the neural network

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:25.010
using the information that we
got from these couple of days

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.840
when we have labeled data.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.970
And we manage to
then find people only

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.384
based on the way they
reflect RF signals.

